   "text": "GLOSSARY/ACRONYMS",
   "html": "<p><strong>GLOSSARY/ACRONYMS </strong></p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "(Updated 02/24/2021)",
   "html": "<p>(Updated 02/24/2021)</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "AAM - Office of Aerospace Medicine",
   "html": "<p><strong>AAM</strong> - Office of Aerospace Medicine</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "AASI - AME Assisted Special Issuance - Criteria under which an AME may reissue a medical certificate for a third-class applicant with a medical history of a disqualifying condition, who has already received a Special Issuance Authorization from the FAA, and criteria to defer issuance to AMCD or RFS for these situations.",
   "html": "<p><strong>AASI</strong> - AME Assisted Special Issuance - Criteria under which an AME may reissue a medical certificate for a third-class applicant with a medical history of a disqualifying condition, who has already received a Special Issuance Authorization from the FAA, and criteria to defer issuance to AMCD or RFS for these situations.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "AMCD - Aerospace Medical Certification Division - located at the Civil Aerospace Medical Institute in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma",
   "html": "<p><strong>AMCD</strong> - Aerospace Medical Certification Division - located at the Civil Aerospace Medical Institute in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "AMCS - Airman Medical Certification System - allows the AME to electronically submit FAA Form 8500-8, Application for Airman Medical Certificate to AMCD.",
   "html": "<p><strong>AMCS</strong> - Airman Medical Certification System - allows the AME to electronically submit FAA Form 8500-8, Application for Airman Medical Certificate to AMCD.</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "page": 761,
   "text": "AME - Aviation Medical Examiner - a physician designated by the FAA and given the authority to perform airman physical examinations for issuance of second- and third-class medical certificates. (NOTE: Senior AMEs perform first-class airman examinations).",
   "html": "<p><strong>AME</strong> - Aviation Medical Examiner - a physician designated by the FAA and given the authority to perform airman physical examinations for issuance of second- and third-class medical certificates. (NOTE: Senior AMEs perform first-class airman examinations).</p>"
  },
